\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlcont\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\f1\fs24\'b7\tab\f0 Horizontal flipping is supported for lines sent to host up to 64 kBytes.\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720 In Area Scan mode, maximum crop height is 65535.\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa200\sl276\slmult1 Historically on X64/Xcelera series, the \b CORACQ_VAL_PIXEL_CLK_PRESENT \b0 status flag represents the Pixel Clock on the Base Camera Link cable.\line In order give a better status to client, in 7.40 this status flag has been renamed \b CORACQ_VAL_PIXEL_CLK_1_PRESENT\b0 . \line Also, we have added the following: \b CORACQ_VAL_PIXEL_CLK_2_PRESENT\b0 , \b CORACQ_VAL_PIXEL_CLK_3_PRESENT \b0 and \b CORACQ_VAL_PIXEL_CLK_ALL_PRESENT\b0 . \line When one wants to check for the clock present before grabbing, the \b CORACQ_VAL_PIXEL_CLK_ALL_PRESENT \b0\line status flag MUST be used as it indicates that the front-end is ready to acquire images.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Buffer Time Stamping has been improved with the addition of the new parameters: \b CORACQ_PRM_TIME_STAMP \b0 and \b CORACQ_PRM_TIME_STAMP_BASE. \b0\line The parameter \b CORXFER_PRM_COUNTER_STAMP_TIME_BASE \b0 is no longer supported. The new parameter \b CORACQ_PRM_TIME_STAMP \b0 permits reading the time stamp, \line resetting the time stamp while the \b CORACQ_PRM_TIME_STAMP_BASE \b0 permits saving in the CCF file the time base.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Board Sync control has been simplified by the addition of 2 new parameters: \b CORACQ_PRM_BOARD_SYNC_OUTPUT1_SOURCE\b0  and \b CORACQ_PRM_BOARD_SYNC_OUTPUT2_SOURCE\b0 . \line These 2 parameters specify the source signal to send to one of the 2 board sync I/Os. The External Frame/Line Trigger source does not specify anymore the board sync as a destination \line (what was called \lquote Pulse to Board Sync\rquote  and \ldblquote To Board Sync\rquote ) in X64/Xcelera series.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}The order in which the Shaft Encoder drop/multiply operations are performed can now be specified using the new parameter: \b CORACQ_PRM_SHAFT_ENCODER_ORDER\b0 .\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}When doing Bi-Color and Bayer conversion using the 80-bit configuration, if the number of camera pixels is not a multiple of 20 bytes, the last pixel of each resulting lines will not have proper pixel value based on the mirror image technique.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}FFC/FLC can be done on lines up to:\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li1080\sa200\sl276\slmult1 64 kBytes: Full and 80-bit configuration\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}16 kBytes: Dual configuration\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa200\sl276\slmult1 FFC/FLC with cluster replacement is not supported for 8 taps/10 bits configuration.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}FFC/FLC maximum gain for 8 taps/10 bits is 2x.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}In 80-bits packed RGB, crop width must be a multiple of 8 pixels.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}In 80-bits packed RGB with 12-bits/pixel, maximum horizontal active allowed is 8192.\ul\b\fs32\par
\ulnone\b0\fs24{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Metadata only available when acquiring into packed host buffers. Not available for planar host buffers.\ul\b\fs32\par
